# 7. API Documentation

All API endpoints are implemented using Next.js Route Handlers.

Base URL:

```text
https://www.saucyculture.in/api
```

## Products API

### GET /api/products

Retrieves all products.

Implementation:

```typescript
prisma.product.findMany({
  orderBy: { id: "asc" }
});
```

Used by the storefront to populate the product catalogue.

## Orders API

### GET /api/orders

Retrieves orders, sorted by creation date in descending order.

Used by the admin dashboard.

### POST /api/orders

Creates a new order.

Expected request data:

```json
{
  "customerName": "Customer Name",
  "customerPhone": "9876543210",
  "shippingAddr": "Full delivery address",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": 1,
      "name": "Product Name",
      "size": "L",
      "qty": 1,
      "price": 1899
    }
  ],
  "totalINR": 1899
}
```

A unique order reference is generated in this format:

```text
SC-IN-123456
```

The initial payment status is:

```text
PAYMENT_ON_HOLD
```

The API currently stores order item details as JSON in `itemsJson`.

### PATCH /api/orders

Updates an order's payment status.

Expected request:

```json
{
  "id": "ORDER_DATABASE_ID",
  "paymentStatus": "COD_CONFIRMED"
}
```

The admin dashboard currently uses these status values:

```text
PAYMENT_ON_HOLD
COD_CONFIRMED
DISPATCHED
```

## Circle API

### GET /api/circle

Retrieves registered VIP members, sorted by newest membership first.

### POST /api/circle

Registers a new VIP member.

Expected request:

```json
{
  "nickname": "Court Nickname",
  "whatsappPhone": "9876543210",
  "preferredSize": "L"
}
```

The API uses Prisma `upsert`.

If the WhatsApp number already exists, the existing member's nickname and preferred size are updated.

The current API returns:

```text
SAUCYVIP10
```

as the VIP code.

