# Final Handover Summary

Saucy Culture is a Next.js-based basketball and streetwear storefront deployed on Vercel, with its source code maintained in GitHub and its production database hosted on Prisma Postgres.

The project currently supports product browsing, search, category filtering, size selection, shopping bag management, COD/payment-hold order creation, VIP community registration, and an owner-facing order/member dashboard.

The production database uses PostgreSQL through Prisma ORM. The website is connected to its custom GoDaddy-registered domain, `saucyculture.in`, with Vercel handling application hosting and SSL.

The next developer should first understand the existing storefront, API routes, database models, and deployment workflow before making changes.

The highest-priority outstanding work is securing administrative and customer-data endpoints, implementing server-side order validation, confirming production product seeding, completing inventory management, and integrating a real payment provider if online payments are required.

**The objective is to maintain a reliable, secure, scalable e-commerce platform while preserving the Saucy Culture brand identity and customer experience.**

